:h2 res=69 id=Invoking_Other_Applications_from_the_IDE.Invoking Other Applications from the IDE
:i1.right button
:i1.mouse, right button
:i1.invoking tools
:i1.Integrated Development Environment, invoking tools
.br
When using the Open Watcom Integrated Development Environment, there are several other applications you may want to use&per. 
 To save you the frustration of having to constantly exit the IDE and start up a new application, we have made it possible 
to invoke other applications from within the Integrated Development Environment&per.  Following are the applications you 
can invoke from the IDE&colon.
:ul compact.
:li.Browser
:li.Open Watcom Debugger
:li.Open Watcom Execution Sampler
:li.Open Watcom Execution Profiler
:li.Open Watcom Disassembler
:li.Open Watcom Editor (text editor)
:li.Open Watcom Resource Editor
:li.Open Watcom Zoom
:li.Open Watcom Heap Walker
:li.Spy
:li.DDE Spy
:eul.
.br
You invoke these applications by making a selection from the toolbar or various menus in the IDE&per.  The Actions menu 
contains some of the applications&per.  You can find others in the Targets and Sources menus&per.  The menu options that 
appear vary, depending on the contents of the current project&per.  The applications are available in the menu items only 
when appropriate&per.  For example, if the currently selected target has no source files, no applications appear in the Sources 
menu&per.
.br
.br
:hp3.Hint&colon.:ehp3.  An alternate way to view the contents of the Targets and Sources menu is to click the right 
mouse button while your cursor is positioned in the project window&per.  If your cursor is positioned over a target, the 
Targets menu appears&per.  If your cursor is positioned over a source file, the Sources menu appears&per.
.br
.br
Refer to the appropriate sections in this manual for detailed information on using the various applications&per.

:h2 res=70 id=Invoking_DOS_Applications_from_the_IDE_under_OSD2.Invoking DOS Applications from the IDE under OS/2
:i1.IDE_DOS_SETTINGS environment variable
:i1.environment variables, IDE_DOS_SETTINGS
:i1.WIN-OS/2 settings
:i1.DOS settings
.br
There are occasions where you may wish to change the default DOS or WIN-OS/2 settings when running a DOS/Windows application 
from the IDE&per.  The mechanism which we provide is through the use of a special:hp2. IDE_DOS_SETTINGS:ehp2. environment 
variable&per.  For example, to set the DPMI memory limit to 16 and to enable DOS BREAK, you can set the environment variable 
as follows&colon.
.br
.br
:hp2.Example&colon.:ehp2.
.br
.br
:font facename=Courier size=12x10.     set ide_dos_settings&eq.dpmi_memory_limit#16;dos_break#1:font facename=Courier size=0x0.
.br
.br
Due to the command processor limitations, the "#" character is used in place of the "&eq."&per.  The above command 
is equivalent to configuring a DOS session with DOS settings as follows&colon.
.br
.br
:font facename=Courier size=12x10.      :font facename=Courier size=0x0.
.br
:font facename=Courier size=12x10.     Variable            Value:font facename=Courier size=0x0.
.br
:font facename=Courier size=12x10.     DPMI_MEMORY_LIMIT   16:font facename=Courier size=0x0.
.br
:font facename=Courier size=12x10.     DOS_BREAK           ON:font facename=Courier size=0x0.

:h2 res=71 id=Using_the_Information_of_the_IDE_from_outside.Using the Information of the IDE from outside
:i1.IDE2MAKE, Utility
:i1.IDE, make
.br
The batch utility IDE2MAKE generates &per.mk and &per.mk1 makefiles for use with Open Watcom Make from the IDE &per.wpj 
and &per.tgt files&per.  See IDE2MAKE in Open Watcom Tools User's Guide&per.

:euserdoc.
